# Review: LibraryPlugin

The plugin is built and the publishing boundary is solid: `Book` carries an `AtprotoRecordAnnotation`
for `buzz.bookhive.book` with a declarative Panproto lens, fields are marked `publish`/`mirror`, and
`book-lens.test.ts` proves private fields never reach the encoded record. The create form offers a
BookHive combobox and autofills the catalog on submit. The biggest divergence is the `Book` type itself:
catalog fields are nested under an inline `catalog` struct, `owned` is published rather than private,
`personalTags`, `format` and a stored `hiveBookUri` do not exist, and `progress` and `content` were added.
The collection card omits reading status, and the article shows the catalog read-only with only the
activity fields editable. No automated test drives the autocomplete create flow. The spec's T-2
(private fields never publish) is not listed by `deus review items`, so it has no verdict here; `book-lens.test.ts`
runs it end to end.

## Extensions

